---
/**
 * I1 facts: why small icons look grey. Explains the rendered stroke width and lists it
 * for every weight at the three small sizes, with the icons drawn at those sizes.
 */
import BoardCell from './BoardCell.astro'
import BoardIcon from './BoardIcon.astro'
import { mapIcon } from './icon-map'
import { SMALL_SIZES, STROKE_ROWS, formatPx, isSubPixel, strokePx } from './stroke-math'

/* EVIDENCE: Chromium at device pixel ratio 1, the calendar glyph on black, 2026-11-20:
   share of lit pixels at 90% white or more. Phosphor Light 16 px: 0%. Regular 16 px: 81%.
   Regular 20 px: 7%. Regular 24 px: 49%. Lucide stroke 1.5 at 16 px: 4%. */
const SAMPLES = ['date', 'chat', 'arrow-next'] as const

const rows = STROKE_ROWS.map((row) => {
  const { set, ...options } = row.style
  return {
    ...row,
    cells: SMALL_SIZES.map((size) => ({
      px: strokePx({ ...row.style, size }) as number,
      icons: SAMPLES.map((name) => mapIcon(name, set, { ...options, size })),
    })),
  }
})
---

<BoardCell wide heading="Dlaczego duże ikony są dobre, a małe szare">
  <div class="stroke-note">
    <ul class="stroke-note__facts">
      <li>
        Ikona to rysunek na siatce, więc kreska kurczy się razem z ikoną. Ta sama waga
        Light ma 6 px w ikonie 128 px i 0,75 px w ikonie 16 px.
      </li>
      <li>
        Zwykły ekran nie zapali części piksela. Kreskę cieńszą niż 1 px rysuje szarym
        pikselem zamiast białego, a kreskę leżącą między pikselami rozmywa na dwa.
      </li>
      <li>
        Opcje A i B mają w małych ikonach kreskę 0,75–1,25 px, która nie trafia w piksele.
        Pomiar na ikonie kalendarza 16 px: Phosphor Light ma 0% w pełni białych pikseli,
        Lucide 4%, Phosphor Regular 81%.
      </li>
      <li>
        Phosphor Regular jest ostry przy 16 px (kreska równo 1 px) i przy 24 px. Rozmiar
        20 px, którego używają dziś przyciski, wypada między pikselami w każdej wadze.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <table class="stroke-table">
      <caption>Grubość kreski na ekranie. Szara liczba: kreska cieńsza niż 1 px.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Waga</th>
          {SMALL_SIZES.map((size) => <th scope="col">{size} px</th>)}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          rows.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">
                {row.label}
                {row.note && <span class="stroke-table__note">{row.note}</span>}
              </th>
              {row.cells.map((cell) => (
                <td>
                  <span class="stroke-table__icons">
                    {cell.icons.map((spec) => (
                      <BoardIcon spec={spec} />
                    ))}
                  </span>
                  <span class:list={['stroke-table__px', isSubPixel(cell.px) && 'is-thin']}>
                    {formatPx(cell.px)}
                  </span>
                </td>
              ))}
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</BoardCell>

<style lang="scss">
  @use '../../../styles/variables' as *;

  .stroke-note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: 2rem 3rem;
    align-items: start;

    @include medium {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .stroke-note__facts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 62ch;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .stroke-table {
    width: 100%;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text);

    caption {
      caption-side: bottom;
      padding-top: 0.75rem;
      text-align: left;
      color: var(--color-text-subtle);
    }

    th {
      font-weight: 400;
      text-align: left;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
    }

    thead th {
      padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
      font-size: var(--text-label);
      letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--color-text-subtle);
    }

    th,
    td {
      padding-block: 0.5rem;
      padding-right: 1rem;
      vertical-align: middle;
    }
  }

  .stroke-table__note {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-subtle);
  }

  .stroke-table__icons {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    min-height: 1.5rem;
  }

  .stroke-table__px {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .stroke-table__px.is-thin {
    color: var(--color-text-subtle);
  }

  @include mobile {
    .stroke-table th,
    .stroke-table td {
      padding-right: 0.5rem;
    }

    .stroke-table__icons {
      gap: 0.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
